+# Washington National Tower package receipt and October FAA tasking
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD07, with PD01–PD04 open. The National Archives **DCA-23** packet contains a signed **October 9, 2003** hand receipt for a Washington National Tower package. The adjoining records give the October 8 certified index, an October 15 rerecording shipment memorandum, an October 16 certification, and an October 22 routing slip. The hand receipt documents an internal FAA intake for the named package. Its wording leaves the exact contents and onward Commission receipt open. [National Archives finding aid, Box 9](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid) · [DCA-23 catalogue](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596243) · [Exact source and test pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Routing and custody fields
+
+| DCA-23 physical page | Source observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| **P. 2, OCR lines 1–20** | The **October 8** certified index lists personnel statements, correspondence, daily facility and traffic-management records, transcripts, notes, emails, fax, voice recordings and position logs. It represents the listed copies as true copies of originals on file at the facility. |
+| **P. 3, lines 1–12 and page face** | The **October 9** signed hand receipt acknowledges a **9-11 Commission package from Washington National Tower**. The signer is the headquarters addressee named in the October 8 directive. The receipt identifies the package by description, with no item-by-item inventory. |
+| **Pp. 4–5, p. 4 lines 29–45 and p. 5 lines 5–46** | The **October 15** memorandum to **ADA-2** says it accompanies shipment of certified rerecording copies. It says the cassette excerpts cover transmissions deemed pertinent, while the original full recordings and certified rerecordings remain on file at the tower. P. 5 gives the separately dated certified index. The scan supplies the sender's statement and the index. |
+| **P. 6, lines 17–19 and 28–48** | The **October 16** certification states that the questions covered on-duty employees from midnight through **11:59 p.m.**, including retired or transferred personnel, subject to exceptions in the attachment. The form distinguishes a required return of government records from encouragement to provide personal notes. |
+| **P. 1, lines 2 and 18–42** | The **October 22** routing slip describes certification statements submitted to **AAT-1 or ADA-2** on **October 8, 15 and 16**, then lists tapes it associates with the October 8 index. Preserve those stated submission dates alongside the separate October 9 receipt. The slip gives no matching receipt for every listed date. |
+
+The October 22 slip lists **15 UTC range labels** and the October 15 certified index lists **36** across the checked lines. They share all six printed **Flight Data Radar** ranges, including the overlapping **1335–1343** and **1340–1350** labels. For **Final 1**, the slip gives **1332–1344** and the index gives **1302–1319** plus **1332–1344**. For **Final 2**, the slip gives **1332–1344** and the index gives **1327–1450** and **1440–1600**, with a two-tape note. These are source inventory labels with distinct scopes. The overlap and count leave the actual number of recordings, export boundaries and contents open. [Range check](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## October 8 directive copies and scope
+
+The October 8 instruction was already held in **ZNY-730** and **AGL-4**. The two new **DCA-19** objects document a separate archive copy path. Both have three physical pages. The scan catalogued as unobstructed shows the **October 8, 2003** memo date on p. 1. The other p. 1 has an overlaid note about a page without obscurities. Both have **OCT-10-2003 12:25** fax imprints in the checked headers. The document date and fax mark identify different fields. The checked pages leave the original send and receipt chain for this particular fax open. [Earlier directive reading](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/4174f2e9c21b8b80967eeb81058a5e97d661c3d0/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-agl-commission-followup-2026-11-08/README.md) · [DCA-19 unobstructed](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596237) · [DCA-19 other copy](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7596238)
+
+Item 3 on physical p. 2 requests the **midnight to 11:59 p.m.** facility population and specifies Potomac personnel who worked at DCA and IAD that day. Item 5 separately describes an **0800–1400 EST** window for particular landline rerecordings. The Cleveland **AWA-772** certification describes a **8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m.** employee-contact window with exceptions. Keep the two directive clauses, the DCA full-day certification and the Cleveland contact wording at their stated levels. The similar six-hour labels leave any link between the Cleveland certification scope and the tape request unestablished. [Cleveland source and prior return comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/71794bb7353a258e0151a7a87a578cf65bcbadb4/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-hq-investigation-and-request-files-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
